<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates nudge higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates nudge higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) rose for the third consecutive session on Monday in anticipation that domestic interest rates will move up, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks are projecting interest rates have now reached bottom,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said, after the Central Bank started selling six-month reverse repos at a higher-than-market rate of 10.125 percent last Thursday.</p>
<p>The same dealer said banks are now funding their peso investments through the swap market where the rates are still low.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  APRIL 7		 APRIL 4</p>
<p>    1 W		9  1/2		  9  7/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  5/8		  9  9/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9 11/16		 9  9/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9  3/4		  9  9/16</p>
<p>    3 M		9 11/16		 9  9/16</p>
<p>    6 M		9 13/16		 9  5/8</p>
<p>    12M		9  7/8		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		8-Apr		   7-Apr</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
